Register the tunnel teardown as soon as the tunnel exists.

ipsec_create() attaches ipsec_on_expire to the contact only when the REGISTER's
Via sent-by port is 5060, so for any other UE the sole remaining place that
attaches it is ims_registrar_pcscf's update_contacts(), on the 200 OK. A
registration that gets its 401, has a tunnel built for it, and then never
completes — the UE gives up, the network drops the second REGISTER, the load
generator times out — therefore has no teardown registered at all. The pending
contact expires on pending_reg_expires and is deleted with the tunnel still
installed: four SAs, four policies and a slot out of ipsec_max_connections, per
abandoned registration. Under load that is a steady drain.

Nothing about the callback depends on the source port, and by this point the
tunnel is created, so attach it unconditionally. is_ulcb_registered() guards
against stacking duplicates when update_contacts() attaches it again on the 200
OK, and on every subsequent re-registration.
diff --git a/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c b/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
index 861f101..77c381e 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_ipsec_pcscf/cmd.c
@@ -1017,14 +1017,19 @@ int ipsec_create(struct sip_msg *m, udomain_t *d, int _cflags)
 		goto cleanup;
 	}
 
-	if(ci.via_port == SIP_PORT) {
-		if(ul.register_ulcb(pcontact,
-				   PCSCF_CONTACT_EXPIRE | PCSCF_CONTACT_DELETE, ipsec_on_expire,
-				   (void *)&pcontact->received_port)
-				!= 1) {
-			LM_ERR("Error subscribing for contact\n");
-			goto cleanup;
-		}
+	// Attach the teardown as soon as the tunnel exists, not only for a UE whose
+	// Via said 5060 and not only once the registration completes: a REGISTER
+	// that is challenged and then never comes back still leaves this tunnel
+	// behind, and the pending contact it belongs to expires without anything
+	// releasing it. is_ulcb_registered() keeps re-registrations from stacking
+	// up duplicate callbacks on the same contact.
+	if(!ul.is_ulcb_registered(pcontact, ipsec_on_expire)
+			&& ul.register_ulcb(pcontact,
+					   PCSCF_CONTACT_EXPIRE | PCSCF_CONTACT_DELETE,
+					   ipsec_on_expire, (void *)&pcontact->received_port)
+					   != 1) {
+		LM_ERR("Error subscribing for contact\n");
+		goto cleanup;
 	}
 
 	ret = IPSEC_CMD_SUCCESS; // all good, set ret to SUCCESS, and exit
